The plugin is a deterministic secret scanner for a Hermes agent: nine provider formats, an entropy heuristic, credential paths, three tools that scan, gate and receipt a decision, and a post-tool-call hook that audits every tool result without changing it. This rewrite keeps all of it and drops the Python: the same rules as cl-ppcre expressions, the same CLEAR/REVIEW/LEAKED verdicts and ALLOW/WARN/BLOCK gates, the same masked-preview-only evidence, the same three tool names, and the audit as advice on Nodecode's :tool point, which hands the result back unaltered exactly as the hook did. The slash command and the tool descriptions are the original's. What was left out: the bundled skill, which the plugin shipped as a file it never registered, so its guidance is the cell's manual topic (help :secret-gate); and the host-state mirror of the receipts, since the cell's ring lives in memory for the life of the process and the event log already holds every tool result the audit read.
